ince-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constrained function object implementing <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;=</span> y</span></code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Nested types","id":"Nested_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::compare_three_way::operator()","id":"std::compare_three_way::operator.28.29"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::compare_three_way","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Function object for performing comparisons."},{"label":"Nested types","children":[{"label":"is_transparent","note":"unspecified"}]},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"operator()","note":"obtains the result of three-way comparison on both arguments"}]},{"label":"std::compare_three_way::operator()","note":"Given the expression std::forward<T>(t) <=> std::forward<U>(u) as expr:","children":[{"label":"Example"},{"label":"Defect reports","note":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards."},{"label":"See also"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":380,"codeBlockCount":2}
